# UI Rules

Before creating a component, search for an existing component that can be reused or extended.

Use:
- primitive UI components
- composite/shared components
- feature-specific components

Keep business-specific components out of generic UI folders.

Every interactive feature should consider:
- loading
- empty
- error
- success
- disabled
- keyboard navigation
- visible focus
- accessible labels
- responsive behavior

Use mobile-first layouts.

Do not use fixed widths when translated text can grow.

User-visible copy must come from **next-intl** message keys — never hardcode strings in UI components.

Use semantic HTML and meaningful alt text.

Use design tokens rather than arbitrary colors, spacing, typography, radius, and shadows.

Prefer CSS logical properties for directional spacing.
